    "body": "## Motivation\n\nThe MUSA FA3 extend path currently selects paged KV-cache attention only when `extend_prefix_lens_cpu` reports a prefix or the batch is in target-verify mode.\n\n`DRAFT_EXTEND_V2` also consumes an existing KV prefix, but that prefix is not represented by the regular extend-prefix condition. Falling through to varlen attention means the draft query can no longer attend to the cached prefix.\n\nThis is a focused upstream port of the fix proven in the MUSA `musa/0.5.16` branch. The original internal change was authored by ning.qiao, who is credited in the commit trailer.\n\n## Modification\n\n- Route MUSA FA3 `DRAFT_EXTEND_V2` batches through `flash_attn_with_kvcache`.\n- Keep the decision in a private MUSA-only helper; no common attention, scheduler, or `ForwardMode` component is changed.\n- Add CPU unit coverage for regular extend, cached-prefix extend, target verify, and draft extend.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `uvx ruff check test/registered/unit/hardware_backend/musa/attention/test_flashattention_draft_extend.py`\n- `uvx ruff format --check python/sglang/srt/hardware_backend/musa/attention/flashattention_backend.py test/registered/unit/hardware_backend/musa/attention/test_flashattention_draft_extend.py`\n- `python3 -m compileall -q` on both changed Python files\n- Focused registered unit test: 4 tests passed\n\nReal-device smoke:\n\n- 1x MTT S5000, host driver 3.3.8-server\n- Image: `registry.mthreads.com/mcconline/inference/sglang:v0.5.16-ph1-4.3.8-torch2.9.0.post1-20260914`\n- Qwen3-8B target + EAGLE3 draft, MUSA FA3, radix cache enabled\n- Target-verify and draft-decode CUDA graphs captured for batch sizes 1 through 8\n- Two identical requests both returned HTTP 200 with response `95`; the repeated request logged 64 cached tokens\n\nThe available production image is tied to v0.5.16, so the device run used this patch backported to the community v0.5.16 checkout together with the backend-instance fix from #46634. The focused unit test above ran against this PR's rebased current-main source.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] The change is limited to the MUSA FA3 backend and its test.\n- [x] The commit is rebased on the latest upstream `main` at submission time.\n- [x] Formatting, static compilation, focused CPU tests, and real MUSA smoke validation passed.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40440407174](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40440407174)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40440406965](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40440406965)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40440407085](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40440407085)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
